## Error Handling

Single error type for the whole app. `thiserror` for clean `Display` impls.

```rust
// error.rs
use thiserror::Error;

#[derive(Debug, Error)]
pub enum AppError {
    #[error("S3 error: {0}")]
    S3(String),

    #[error("Connection not found: {id}")]
    ConnectionNotFound { id: String },

    #[error("Invalid credentials")]
    InvalidCredentials,

    #[error("IO error: {0}")]
    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),

    #[error("Serialization error: {0}")]
    Serde(#[from] serde_json::Error),

    #[error("Keyring error: {0}")]
    Keyring(String),
}

impl AppError {
    pub fn into_string(self) -> String {
        self.to_string()
    }
}
```

- Never `unwrap()` or `expect()` in command or service code — always propagate with `?`
- `expect()` is allowed only in `main.rs` / `lib.rs` startup where a panic is intentional
- Never return raw SDK error strings to the frontend — map them to `AppError` variants first

