## Naming Conventions

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files | `snake_case` | `bucket.rs`, `client.rs` |
| Functions | `snake_case` | `list_objects`, `build_client` |
| Types / Structs | `PascalCase` | `BucketFile`, `AppState` |
| Tauri commands | `snake_case` (matches frontend invoke key) | `list_files`, `upload_file` |
| Errors | `PascalCase` variant, descriptive | `ConnectionNotFound`, `InvalidCredentials` |
| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_UPLOAD_CHUNK_SIZE` |

---

## Do Not

- Do not write business logic in `main.rs` or `lib.rs`
- Do not call AWS SDK methods outside `s3/operations.rs`
- Do not `unwrap()` or `expect()` in commands or services
- Do not duplicate a function — if it exists somewhere, import it
- Do not let any file exceed 500 lines — split and re-export
- Do not return raw error strings from SDK — always map to `AppError`
- Do not store secrets in plain app config — use `keyring` via `storage/credentials.rs`
